{
  "$meta": {
    "description": "Shadows and elevation. Apple shadows are soft, large, low alpha, and always paired with a hairline edge. Values from the macOS 27 and iOS 27 kits unless marked.",
    "sources": {
      "kit": "macOS 27 Windows, Panels, Knobs layer styles; iOS 27 Controls",
      "estimate": "verify visually"
    },
    "reconciledDate": "2026-11-27"
  },
  "rules": [
    "Content layer elements (cards, rows) have NO shadow on iOS. Separation comes from background level (grouped vs secondary).",
    "Shadows belong to floating things: windows, panels, menus, popovers, sheets, glass bars, toggle and slider knobs.",
    "Every floating surface has a hairline edge: 0 0 0 0.5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08 to 0.2) light, rgba(255,255,255,0.1 to 0.2) dark.",
    "Dark mode shadows are stronger in alpha but you also lighten the surface (elevated background). Never rely on shadow alone in dark mode.",
    "Inactive macOS windows use the inactive shadow (smaller, lighter)."
  ],
